  "body": "The punctured complex E8 copy-cost floor from PR968/PR1077 was stated for exactly\neight terms. This structural research proof extends the same lower bound,\nmax(72-p,56) for p<=24, to any finite number of active terms provided both factor\nmatrices remain in the live root code. More terms in that class cannot improve\nthe prior attaining curve or its best 7/13 ratio.\n\nThe new argument uses rank counting and handles the exceptional p8/m9 case by\na positive inverse-Gram diagonal contradiction. An exact nine-term factorization\nwith outside-code columns demonstrates why unrestricted overcomplete decoders\nremain open. The inherited real-flat classification is explicitly retained.\n\nStandard-library replay checks the source-bound predecessor geometric facts,\nfour complex overcomplete examples over all root pairs and 25 punctures,\n1024 root-pair costs, 16 rational Gram certificates, a 12544-entry outside-code\nidentity, five mathematical controls and six package mutations. Reproduction,\nproof, source pins, exact receipt and predecessor credit are in the package.\n\nNo physical decoder construction, unrestricted factorization lower bound, native\nadmission or new kappa is claimed. Only one new research directory is added;\nselected PR1094 and upstream remain unchanged. Credit belongs to PR968/1077 and\ntheir retained geometric lineage; PR765 and 1071 are distinguished explicitly.\nPrepared for @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, Apache-2.0.\n",
